      "orig": "     <PCE-initiated-lsp-request> ::= (<PCE-initiated-lsp-instantiation>|\n                                      <PCE-initiated-lsp-deletion>)\n\n     <PCE-initiated-lsp-instantiation> ::= <SRP>\n                                           <LSP>\n                                           [<END-POINTS>]\n                                           <ERO>\n                                           [<attribute-list>]\n\n     <PCE-initiated-lsp-deletion> ::= <SRP>\n                                      <LSP>",
      "correct": "     <PCE-initiated-lsp-request> ::= (<PCE-initiated-lsp-instantiation>|\n                                      <PCE-initiated-lsp-deletion-or-reclamation>)\n\n     <PCE-initiated-lsp-instantiation> ::= <SRP>\n                                           <LSP>\n                                           [<END-POINTS>]\n                                           <ERO>\n                                           [<attribute-list>]\n\n     <PCE-initiated-lsp-deletion-or-reclamation> ::= <SRP>\n                                                     <LSP>",
      "notes": "Update needed to solve ambiguity for any extra object included after SRP and LSP objects in reclaim delegation request, which is coming from:\n\nhttps://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc8281#section-6\nA PCE (either the original or one of its backups) sends a PCInitiate\n   message that includes just the SRP and LSP objects and carries the\n   PLSP-ID of the LSP it wants to take control of."
    }
